text:
mara: Posting a quick mobile UX find from today's console pass — when you open the left sidebar on narrow widths it slides over but the main table's sticky header jumps down ~8px. Screenshot: https://img.redwood.test/console/2026-03-sidebar-jump.png

devin: repro'd on iPhone 12 simulator. Happens when sidebar animation finishes. Looks like the header gets reflowed, maybe because of transform-translate + position:sticky interplay.

sandeep: Could be because we add a backdrop element with `height: 100vh` while the header is still sticky. Quick hack: `backdrop { position: fixed; inset: 0; }` but need to check stacking context.

lia: UX thought — on very small screens we should avoid the overlay slide entirely and use a bottom sheet pattern for actions; sidebar is heavy. Any objections to switching at <= 420px? :thinking:

mara: I like bottom sheet for actions, but we still need access to the route-level nav. Bottom sheet could be for filters/columns only. Side nav needed for switching projects.

devin: OK split: <= 420px filters/columns as bottom sheet; 421-680px keep slide-over nav but make it full-screen modal (no simultaneous sticky header). That avoids header jumps. We can shove that logic into our breakpoint tokens.

sandeep: Suggested CSS snippet for reference:```css
@media (max-width: 420px) {
  .console-sidebar { position: fixed; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 56vh; border-top-left-radius: 12px; }
}
@media (min-width: 421px) and (max-width: 680px) {
  .console-sidebar { position: fixed; inset: 0; height: 100vh; }
  .main-header { position: relative; }
}
```

lia: Accessibility nit — if we do full-screen modal at 421-680, ensure focus trap and `aria-hidden` on main content. Also keyboard ESC should close both bottom sheet and full-screen nav.

mara: Agreed. Another copy/UI nit: the column toggle currently says `Show columns` but it's a persistent preference. Suggest rename to `Columns & density` and include a small description line. Devin, can you surface that in the bottom sheet?

devin: Yep — will add a two-line header: `Columns & density
Choose visible columns and row density (saved per-device)` — small text-muted. Also will add `role="dialog" aria-describedby` for screen readers.

sandeep: Table overflow: when we switch to stacked rows at narrow width, long token strings (like model IDs) are overflowing and causing horizontal scroll. Suggest wrapping with break-all on the token cells and maybe show a truncated pill with copy-to-clipboard.

lia: For hit targets — tap areas on the compact table rows are ~28px; we need to hit 44px min. We should make the primary row tap target (whole tile) and leave smaller icon buttons as secondary. This will reduce accidental taps on the kebab.

mara: Can we add a small A/B for 2 weeks? Variant A: stacked cards with full-row tap target. Variant B: compact table with increased row padding to 44px min. Metrics: tap success, navigation time, accidental kebab opens.

devin: I'll wire up flags. Quick question: should the header keep the search bar on narrow screens or hide behind a magnifier icon? Current layout steals space from title.

lia: Hide it behind an icon at <= 480px. Provide a visible label for the icon: `aria-label="Open search"`. Screen reader users should get the search field directly after activating.

ui-bot: Reminder: update design tokens doc (sources/design/tokens.md) if we change breakpoint values.

mara: Thanks all — action items: Devin add breakpoint logic + copy tweak; Sandeep wrap long tokens + clipboard pill; Lia accessibility checklist; Mara to draft A/B plan and schedule a short usability session with 6 folks. I'll post follow-up with PR links. :thumbsup:
